# Inkwell Studio bridge — image backend config.
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own key. Never commit `.env`.

IMAGE_BACKEND=stub
# IMAGE_BACKEND=openai
# IMAGE_URL=https://api.together.xyz
# IMAGE_MODEL=Rundiffusion/Juggernaut-Lightning-Flux
# IMAGE_SIZE=1024x768
# IMAGE_STEPS=4
# IMAGE_KEY=your-key-here

# --- notes ---
# • stub (default): a real image generated locally from the prompt — a mood-board
#   gradient with the prompt text. Zero setup; not model art.
# • openai backend: OpenAI-compatible /v1/images/generations (Together AI, DashScope
#   Qwen-Image, local, hosted...). IMAGE_CONCURRENCY (default 2) and IMAGE_RETRIES
#   (default 3, retries 429/5xx with backoff) also apply.
# • Together retired its free FLUX.1-schnell serverless tier (as of 2026-10); the model
#   above is its cheapest current serverless option (~$0.0017/image). Run
#   `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $IMAGE_KEY" https://api.together.xyz/v1/models` and
#   filter for `"type": "image"` to see what's currently available/priced on your key.
# • a1111 backend: Automatic1111 / SD.Next POST {IMAGE_URL}/sdapi/v1/txt2img

# --- narration ("Read story aloud") ---
# Edge TTS (server/narrate.py) — needs outbound internet to Microsoft's TTS endpoint; no
# fallback voice if it's unreachable. Uncomment to override the defaults:
# TTS_VOICE=en-US-AnaNeural
# TTS_RATE=-8%
# TTS_TIMEOUT=20
